      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #100(g)): an error raised by a *primitive*
      ⍝ operand called from inside a multi-chunk f⍤y (which -- unlike
      ⍝ the single-chunk fast path a few lines below -- always goes
      ⍝ through Macro::MAC_Z__LO_RANK_X5_B, primitive or not) used to
      ⍝ show a single, degenerate caret landing on the derived
      ⍝ function's own opening '(' regardless of which operand cell
      ⍝ actually failed. Widened to the whole statement containing that
      ⍝ degenerate point (Error.cc's update_error_info()), which here
      ⍝ brackets the derived-function application itself.
      ⍝ The left caret is at the start of the statement: its range used to
      ⍝ end at the statement's END token, which has no counterpart in the
      ⍝ unoptimized statement, so the caret landed on ⍳. The right caret
      ⍝ is at the folded 2 2⍴'ab'.
      ⍝
      (⍳⍤1)2 2⍴'ab'
DOMAIN ERROR
      (⍳⍤1)2 2⍴'ab'
